<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Earhart returns five and a half weeks after left endoscopic sinus surgery, done as day surgery without complications. She needed acetaminophen for about a week and no stronger painkiller. Dr. Lindgren cleaned the sinus cavities in the otolaryngology clinic at one and three weeks; at three weeks the left maxillary opening, ethmoid cavity and frontal recess were open and healing, she could clear her ears normally, and he cleared her to fly. She has since flown four times as pilot without any pressure pain on descent. Her nose is clear on most days, her smell is coming back, and she sleeps through the night. She rinses with saline and budesonide every morning and with plain saline at night. The pathology showed chronic inflammation without many eosinophils, with no fungus and no tumor. SNOT-22 today 12. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Surgery</td><td>Left endoscopic sinus surgery five and a half weeks ago, without complications</td></tr><tr><td>Healing</td><td>Cavities open and healing at the three-week cleaning</td></tr><tr><td>Flying</td><td>Cleared at three weeks; four flights without pressure pain</td></tr><tr><td>Scores</td><td>SNOT-22 12; facial pain 1 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Pathology</td><td>Chronic inflammation, few eosinophils, no fungus, no tumor</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

